00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:06.309 align:start position:0%
our councils started to review our  planning enforcement procedures in 2019  with the main aim of enhancing customer  experience  we also wanted to improve efficiency and  performance  and subsequently formed a framework of  tasks for officers to help achieve this  we have undertaken a thorough review of  our planning enforcement process  from receipt of customer report to  completion to help identify  strengths and weaknesses this has also  included an evaluation of case  management  specialized software was used to map out  the planning enforcement lifecycle  this enabled us to exclude unnecessary  steps  improving efficiency and resulting in a  better customer experience  to build on this further we incorporated  markers for customer contact into the  process  ensuring the team provided regular  updates to customers  as reports progressed case management  task triggers were also created to aid  performance and efficiency  we then consulted with councillors and  other stakeholders on the proposed  improvements  to ensure that these best met the needs  of customers in our districts  changes to procedures have paved the way  for ongoing  improvements in speed efficiency and  handling of a planning enforcement  report from  start to finish we have seen significant  results to date  and the process continues to evolve  meeting our aim to provide a  customer-centric service  that delivers the desired outcomes  our customers have already benefited  from a more efficient service  last year we achieved a reduction of 23  per cent in the number of cases  that have been ongoing for longer than  six months  we hope to see a bigger decrease this  year following the implementation of  software to assist  officers in managing cases according to  stated time scales  and customer expectations  a business intelligence application  crystal reports  has also been introduced to aid case  management and  monitoring this is currently used by  other colleagues in the planning team  and has proved very successful so far  we are confident that the changes to our  procedures have already  increased performance and efficiency  however  our councils remain committed to  continually improving our planning  enforcement service  and customer experience to enable us to  do this  we will undertake regular reviews of our  processes  assessing effectiveness and implementing  further improvements if required  you
 

